.TH PORELO-HOST 8 "2026-11-09" "Porelo" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
porelo-host \- the host's own program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B porelo-host
.RB [ \-\-help " | " \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B porelo-host
is run by sudo rules granting NOPASSWD access for the calling person alone,
or by root's systemd service and socket units.
It is never typed directly by a person in a shell.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B org status [\-\-json]
Root's read of the last applied organization, persons, projects, repositories,
and their last measured central state. Refused when SUDO_USER is set.
Takes a shared flock on /etc/porelo-host/forge.conf and contacts no network.
With \-\-json, prints one complete JSON object in the host protocol's field order.
Otherwise prints the host, organization state, person count, and project count.
.TP
.B task show <fingerprint>
Prints the complete recorded task certificate as one JSON object.
Root without SUDO_USER can read any person's task records.
Through sudo, the calling SUDO_USER must be recorded, unlocked and not revoked
by the organization. Any task whose principal task:<project>:<task> names a
project the caller belongs to is visible, using membership from the host's
people records. A task outside those projects is refused with status 65 and
exactly the same output as an unrecorded fingerprint.
Takes an exclusive flock on forge.conf.
The fingerprint must match SHA256: followed by exactly 43 base64 characters,
without padding. No certificate or token is created or changed.
.TP
.B task sweep
Root's timer only; refused with status 65 when SUDO_USER is set.
Takes an exclusive flock on /etc/porelo-host/forge.conf, retries pending person
locks, and deletes forge task tokens whose recorded certificate has ended.
Retains every task record and every token for a task whose certificate is still valid.
Prints one JSON object with a sorted swept list of login/task names.
One person's forge failure stops no other person's sweep; failures answer status
69, naming the completed deletions and failures. Removal of the temporary
administrator token is attempted before the answer, including when a request
fails; a cleanup failure refuses the call.
.TP
.B task start <task>
Through sudo only: read one Ed25519 task certificate from bounded standard input.
Require the calling person's current organization key, a single principal
 task:<project>:<task>, current validity, and membership of that project.
The installed porelo judges it again against that key and the host KRL in an
isolated systemd unit. Record the certificate privately before making the gate
 token; answer the token alone without a line end, or nothing on a forge-less host.
An identical certificate is a retry and rotates its token. Another certificate
for that task, or the same task key recorded elsewhere, is refused.
.TP
.B task end <task>
Through sudo only: delete that task's gate token alone, retain its certificate,
and print {"task":"<task>","ended":true}. An unrecorded task is refused.
.TP
.B forge issue\-token
Through sudo only: replace the person's forge tokens except lends younger than
one day, and answer the new token alone, without a line end.
.TP
.B forge lend\-token
Through sudo only: make a token for one command, preserving the person's token
and every lend younger than one day. Delete older or unreadable lends.
Answer the new token alone, without a line end.
.PP
These four verbs take an exclusive flock on forge.conf for authorization,
record publication and forge changes. They take the person from SUDO_USER only.
A temporary administrator token is deleted before answering, even on failure.
No certificate or token is put on a command line or in a diagnostic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help. Available to any uid with an accepted environment.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the Porelo build version. Available to any uid with an accepted environment.
.SH BOUNDARY
The environment is checked before argument parsing, including help and version.
Only the names sudo's env_reset keeps by default and those systemd sets for a
service or a socket are accepted; none of them reaches a child program, and the
program's own locale and output encoding are fixed.
The complete name allow-list is:
.nf
SUDO_USER SUDO_UID SUDO_GID SUDO_COMMAND SUDO_HOME HOME PATH
LOGNAME USER SHELL MAIL TERM LANG COLUMNS LINES INVOCATION_ID
JOURNAL_STREAM NOTIFY_SOCKET LISTEN_FDS LISTEN_PID
LISTEN_FDNAMES RUNTIME_DIRECTORY STATE_DIRECTORY
CACHE_DIRECTORY LOGS_DIRECTORY CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY
CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY SYSTEMD_EXEC_PID MANAGERPID
WATCHDOG_PID WATCHDOG_USEC USERNAME SUDO_TTY
MEMORY_PRESSURE_WATCH MEMORY_PRESSURE_WRITE MAINPID PIDFILE
SERVICE_RESULT EXIT_CODE EXIT_STATUS TRIGGER_UNIT
TRIGGER_PATH TRIGGER_TIMER_REALTIME_USEC
TRIGGER_TIMER_MONOTONIC_USEC MONITOR_SERVICE_RESULT
MONITOR_EXIT_CODE MONITOR_EXIT_STATUS MONITOR_INVOCATION_ID
MONITOR_UNIT REMOTE_ADDR REMOTE_PORT LANGUAGE LINGUAS
_XKB_CHARSET TZ COLORS COLORTERM LS_COLORS DISPLAY XAUTHORITY
XAUTHORIZATION XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP HOSTNAME KRB5CCNAME PS1 PS2
LC_*
.fi
Unknown names are refused with the variable's name, never its value:
a widened sudo env_keep is a broken host configuration.
Accepted variables do not configure behavior; SUDO_USER and SUDO_UID identify
the person, and socket activation variables are reserved for later verbs.
HOME, PATH and directory variables are never used to locate configuration.
.PP
A person is taken only from SUDO_USER, never from an argument.
The login must be a non-root account and SUDO_UID must match the system account database.
Missing, empty, invalid, unknown or mismatching identities are refused.
Root's unit invocations need no person until a verb acts for one.
.PP
Other invocations require real uid 0.
Argument files are not expanded and JVM runtime options are ordinary arguments.
Child programs are checked through SystemProgram, run without a shell from /,
with a fixed locale: LANG=C.UTF-8 for task work, LC_ALL=C for project work.
Children use PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin; nothing under /usr/local is run.
Command output is bounded. Person account lookup has no deadline; maintenance
commands take at most 60 seconds. Project transfers keep their own deadlines.
Root-owned data files must be regular files without symbolic links;
the file and every parent through / must be root-owned and not writable
by group or others, including sticky temporary directories.
Reads are bounded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 64 (EX_USAGE)
Invalid arguments, no verb, or a task start/end or forge token call without SUDO_USER.
.TP
.B 65 (EX_DATAERR)
Invalid host records or project data, a root-only verb called through sudo,
no visible task, a refused task/token caller, or a refused forge operation.
.TP
.B 69 (EX_UNAVAILABLE)
A required dependency or account database could not answer.
Task and forge verbs also return this status when not root, as do project verbs
other than check-central.
.TP
.B 73 (EX_CANTCREAT)
A task path is unsafe, or the host's files or configuration lock could not be read.
.TP
.B 77 (EX_NOPERM)
Root uid or a valid sudo person could not be established.
.TP
.B 78 (EX_CONFIG)
The invocation environment contains an unapproved variable.
.SS Codes by verb
Shared boundary codes: 77 no valid root or sudo person; 78 unapproved environment variable.
.TP
.B org status
0 status shown; 64 bad arguments; 65 sudo or invalid records;
69 unsafe or unreadable host files; 73 lock or unhandled file/data failure.
.TP
.B org follow
0 followed or read key not yet added; 64 bad arguments; 65 sudo, invalid pin, records or signed state;
69 host file, dependency, deadline or reconciliation failure; 73 unsafe path, lock, publication or unhandled file/data failure.
.TP
.B org refresh
0 refreshed; 64 bad arguments; 65 sudo, invalid or unexpected token, pin, records or signed state;
69 host file, dependency, deadline or reconciliation failure; 73 unsafe path, input, lock, publication or unhandled file/data failure.
.TP
.B org renew\-pin
0 pins replaced and status shown; 64 bad arguments; 65 sudo, invalid pins, no organization or invalid records;
69 unsafe or unreadable host files; 73 unsafe path, input, lock, publication or unhandled file/data failure.
.TP
.B task show
0 record shown; 64 bad arguments or fingerprint; 65 caller, records or visibility refused;
69 not root or file/account lookup failure; 73 unsafe task path, lock or file failure.
.TP
.B task sweep
0 sweep complete; 64 bad arguments; 65 sudo or invalid records;
69 not root, dependency, revocation or forge failure; 73 unsafe task path, lock or file failure.
.TP
.B task start
0 task recorded and token answered, if enabled; 64 bad arguments, input form or no SUDO_USER;
65 caller, certificate or task conflict; 69 not root, file, dependency or forge failure;
73 unsafe task path, recording, lock or file failure.
.TP
.B task end
0 token ended; 64 bad arguments, task name or no SUDO_USER; 65 caller, records or unknown task;
69 not root, file, dependency or forge failure; 73 unsafe task path, lock or file failure.
.TP
.B forge issue\-token, forge lend\-token
0 token answered; 64 bad arguments or no SUDO_USER; 65 caller or records refused;
69 not root, no forge, file, dependency or forge failure; 73 lock or unhandled file failure.
.TP
.B project add
0 registered; 64 bad arguments/signing key or interrupted registration;
65 registration, data, inherited lock or forge refusal;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 file/output write failure.
.TP
.B project remove
0 removed; 64 bad arguments/central token or interrupted push check;
65 project, data, inherited lock, forge refusal or unpushed work;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 file/output write failure.
.TP
.B project migrate
0 migrated; 64 bad arguments/JSON; 65 project, address, key, inherited lock or forge refusal;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 file/output write failure.
.TP
.B project take\-off
0 removed; 64 bad arguments/JSON; 65 project, data, inherited lock, forge refusal or unpushed work;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 file/output write failure.
.TP
.B project central\-state
0 state shown, including cannot-say; 64 bad arguments; 65 project, data or inherited lock refused;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 output write failure.
.TP
.B project give\-back\-check
0 all mains at central; 64 bad arguments; 65 data, wrong lock or main not known to be at central;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 output write failure.
.TP
.B project project\-copy
0 copy or unchanged main; 64 bad arguments; 65 project, address, data or inherited lock refused;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 directory creation or output write failure.
.TP
.B project project\-advance
0 comparison reported; 64 bad arguments; 65 project, changed copy, data or inherited lock refused;
69 not root, dependency/read/lock, Git or cleanup failure; 73 file/output write failure.
.TP
.B project check\-central
0 all commits at central; 64 bad arguments/oversized token; 65 CA path or unpushed work;
66 local token unreadable/empty or unsafe CA; 69 dependency/configuration/read/Git failure;
73 diagnostic write failure; 75 no central token; 77 sudo invocation.
.TP
.B project measure\-central
0 published, possibly empty; 64 bad arguments; 65 project, data or inherited lock refused;
69 not root or local dependency/read/lock failure; 73 publication, ACL or diagnostic write failure.
.TP
.B project pool\-key send
0 key sent or already current; 64 bad arguments; 65 project data, inherited lock or forge refusal;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 marker or output write failure.
.TP
.B project pool\-key withdraw
0 withdrawn, absent or forge gone; 64 bad arguments; 65 data, wrong lock or forge refusal;
69 not root or dependency/read/lock failure; 73 output write failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/porelo-host/
Root's forge.conf, people records and organization state, pin and project progress.
.TP
.B /var/lib/porelo-host/tasks/<login>/<task>.json
Root's private, durable task certificate records.
.TP
.B /usr/sbin/porelo-host
The host program.
.TP
.B /proc/self/status
Kernel source of the real uid.
.TP
.B /proc/self/uid_map
Namespace mapping used for root-owned file and program checks.
.TP
.B /proc/sys/kernel/overflowuid
Owner uid reported for an unmapped host root.
.TP
.B /etc/nsswitch.conf
The system account database configuration used by getent passwd.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR porelo (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR systemd (1),
.BR getent (1)
.SH PROJECT COMMANDS
.TP
.B project add <project> <admin> \-\-signed-by <key>
Register a project named for this admin in the applied organization.
The canonical Ed25519 signing key is pinned in root's private record.
The organization gets its teams and an isolated package publisher.
.TP
.B project remove <project>
Check every repository ref against central before deleting this project's
repositories, packages, organization, publisher, memberships and publications.
A partial removal keeps its record for retry.
.TP
.B project migrate <project>
Read one JSON object containing address and token from standard input.
Migrate the repository, install a read-only deploy key and protect main.
The token stays in memory and the private forge request.
.TP
.B project take-off <project>
Read one JSON object containing repository and token (or null) from stdin.
Check all work before deleting the repository and its read key.
Without a token, report the central deploy key for its owner to remove.
.TP
.B project central-state <project>
Print the compact JSON central-state record without making an admin token.
Every repository is up-to-date, ahead, moved-on or cannot-say.
.TP
.B project pool-key send|withdraw
Send /var/lib/porelo-host/pool/run-key as the PORELO_POOL_SSH organization
secret to registered projects, or withdraw only that secret.
Send again when the key changes or an organization lacks it; record its SHA-256
in run-key.sent only after every upload succeeds. The key and marker are private.
Print compact JSON containing the sorted changed project names.
Withdrawal succeeds without making a token when forge.conf, the forge account,
or the answering forge is gone. An answering forge's refusal stops withdrawal.
.PP
Every project verb except check-central accepts a trailing \-\-lock-fd <descriptor> for the
follow's existing exclusive flock on the trusted forge.conf open description.
Private records have mode 0600, their directories 0700.
A write failure exits 73; data refusal exits 65; unavailable dependencies exit 69.
.TP
.B project give-back-check
Check every registered project's main before returning the host.
Refuse when any main is ahead, moved-on, or cannot-say; remove nothing.
.TP
.B project project-copy <project> <address> <known-commit|->
Read central main using the repository's read key and pinned SSH host keys.
Remove old copies; return a private bare copy owned by the forge account,
or a null copy when main is unchanged. The enclosing directory has mode 0711.
.TP
.B project project-advance <project> <repository> <commit> <copy> <signed|tip>
Bundle the copy as its owner and advance the forge's main only forward.
The signed reach takes only project.yml changes or an exact Porelo-Signs-Anew
trailer for that file. The tip reach follows unused repositories, except those
holding workflows or naming snippet_file. Tell Forgejo after moving the ref.
Print up-to-date, moved, ahead, diverged, other-changes or moved-unseen as JSON.
A changed copy exits 65; a Git or cleanup failure exits 69.
.TP
.B project check-central <project> <repository>...
Root without sudo only: compare every local ref with central reachability.
Read migrated original_url values over /run/porelo-forge/git.sock and clone
from the token gate on literal 127.0.0.1 at forge.conf's git_port.
Read the central token from stdin without echo and the local token as its owner;
no token enters argv or diagnostics. Refuse unpushed commits with 65.
Use forge/central-ca.conf or the system CA bundle for central only and refuse
redirects. Neither forge is written. This verb takes no inherited lock fd.
.TP
.B project measure-central <project>
Publish the comparison to organization/central/<project>.json with the follow's
project, read_at and repositories fields, spaced JSON and a trailing newline.
Grant read access only to the applied project's unlocked, admitted members
whose local accounts exist. Replace the old file's readers before asking central.
A failed question publishes an empty list, never an up-to-date answer.

.SS org follow
Follow the signed organization from root's timer. Requires root without SUDO_USER.
Fetch and validate the complete state before changing access. Removed readers lose
access before slow service and central questions. Project operations run in this
process under the host configuration lock. The whole follow has five minutes;
project-file reads share sixty seconds and central measurements share 120 seconds.
.SS org refresh
Follow immediately from the window over root's SSH connection. The central token
arrives on standard input alone, at most 4096 bytes, for adding the host's read key
or a waiting migration. Empty input follows without migrating. A token nobody
waits for is refused. The result is the complete organization status as JSON.
.SS org renew-pin
Take one login and canonical SSH key per line on standard input from root on the
machine. Duplicate keys and malformed lines are refused. The pin is replaced
atomically and the saved fetch refusal is cleared; the accepted revision remains.
